-money-bankers-rounding-fin-212-08d3cd5986", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 371322, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_019UhJZWpo3dL7rf1pJYzpGx", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 373164, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "The fix is in a pull request for review: https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101\n\n- **Root cause:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP`. FIN-212 and the function's own docstring require `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`.\n- **Change:** Switched the rounding mode to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN` on branch `fix/money-bankers-rounding-fin-212` (commit `08d3cd5986`). It's a one-line change.\n- **CI:** Run `ci-0001` passed on that commit.\n- **PR:** Opened against `main` with alex as reviewer. Its description notes the test values check out under half-even (2.675\u21922.68, 2.665\u21922.66).\n\nI didn't merge it. Merging into main needs approval from a code owner, so the PR is waiting on that.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I'll start by reading the source and the test to see what's expected.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01TcZB1QMqDvzYZH8ACwMtU4", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "src/money.py", "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_018W2Wz5KuRDuA1Ey2gqVoRe", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "tests/test_money.py", "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The bug is clear: `round_money` uses `ROUND_HALF_UP`, but the docstring and FIN-212 call for `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. The test's expected values (2.675\u21922.68, 2.665\u21922.66) match half-even. I'll create the branch and commit the one-line